<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Juliomagus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Angers is a city on the Maine river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the historic capital of Anjou. As Juliomagus it was the chief town of the Gallic Andecavi under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, later taking their name. It was the seat of the counts of Anjou, whose line produced the Plantagenet kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and its 13th-century castle houses the Apocalypse Tapestry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angers.jpg" alt="Angers" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174, etc. (see above) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Angers_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
